<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Hire purchase: working back to the deposit (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A {@item@} has a cash price of Ksh \( {@C0@} \). Its hire purchase price is \( {@ep@}\% \) higher than the cash price. A buyer pays a deposit and then \( {@n0@} \) monthly instalments of Ksh \( {@x0@} \).</p>
<p>(a) Find the hire purchase price.</p>
<div>Hire purchase price \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Find the deposit paid.</p>
<div>Deposit \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) What percentage of the hire purchase price was the deposit?</p>
<div>[[input:ans3]] \( \% \) [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> \( H = {@C0@} + \frac{ {@ep@} }{100} \times {@C0@} = {@C0@} \times {@float(1 + ep/100)@} = {@H0@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> The instalments total \( {@x0@} \times {@n0@} = {@x0*n0@} \). Since \( H = D + xn \),</p>
\[ D = H - xn = {@H0@} - {@x0*n0@} = {@D0@}. \]
<p><strong>(c)</strong> \( \dfrac{ {@D0@} }{ {@H0@} } \times 100\% = {@rd(dpc)@}\% \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[rd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else float(v);
item : rand(["refrigerator", "cooker", "television", "bicycle", "wardrobe"]);
cands : sublist(create_list([u, w, v, f], u, [30000, 40000, 50000, 60000, 80000], w, [10, 15, 20, 25], v, [8, 10, 12, 15], f, [20, 25, 30, 40]),
  lambda([z], block([h], h : z[1]*(1 + z[2]/100), integerp(h*(1 - z[4]/100)/z[3]))));
pk : rand(cands);
C0 : pk[1];
ep : pk[2];
n0 : pk[3];
H0 : C0*(1 + ep/100);
D0 : H0*pk[4]/100;
x0 : (H0 - D0)/n0;
dpc : 100*D0/H0;
w_fromC : C0 - x0*n0;                     /* used the cash price instead of the HP price */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
